# BLoC

- One folder per bloc. `*_bloc.dart` has `part` of `*_event.dart`, `*_state.dart`, `*_bloc.freezed.dart`.
- Events: `@freezed sealed class`. State: `@freezed abstract class`. Both `part of 'the_bloc.dart';`.
- `on<TheEvent>` then `await event.when(...)`. Inject use cases, not repositories.
- State: `DataStatus` (`none`, `loading`, `success`, `error`) plus domain data / `BaseFailure?`.
- Load in **`State.initState`** with `context.read<TheBloc>()` (safe). Never `add` in `build`. `context.watch` is not allowed in `initState`.

```dart
final bloc = context.read<CatalogItemsBloc>();
if (bloc.state.status == DataStatus.none) {
  bloc.add(const CatalogItemsEvent.getCatalogItems());
}
```

- Navigate in `BlocListener` / `BlocConsumer` on the screen that should react. Use `listenWhen` so login success and sign-out success are not treated as the same.
- Auth `signIn` calls `SignInUseCase` (email `test@user.com` + password `Test1234`). On success, `await Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 2))` then `DataStatus.success`. `signOut` is still a 2s delayed stub.
- Order Summary `initState` dispatches `CartEvent.fulfillPayment()`. The bloc waits 10s, then `UpdatePaymentUseCase` sets `fulfilled: true`. Skip if already fulfilled or `fulfillmentRequested`.
